  "title": "FreeCalc Lite",
  "summary": "Count calories and macros from barcodes or your own foods, on your phone only.",
  "description": "Keep a food diary without signing up for anything. Scan a barcode to find a food you saved before, look a product up online when you allow it, or pick from the built-in list of generic foods. Each diary entry works out calories, protein, carbs and fat from its serving size.\n\n- **Today at a glance:** calories against your daily goal, and the macros of the day.\n- **Trends:** 7-day and 30-day charts and your daily average.\n- **Your foods:** save a food once and reuse it with any serving size.\n\n**What it never does:** no ads, no tracking and no account. The diary stays on this phone. Only a scanned barcode leaves it, and only when you look a product up online.",
  "license": "MIT",
